# Feature state folder

Every Flutter app in this monorepo that uses feature folders keeps **state** and **provider/notifier** in separate files under `state/`.

## Layout

```
lib/features/<feature>/
  state/
    <feature>_state.dart       # immutable state (+ enums used only by that state)
    <feature>_provider.dart    # ChangeNotifier (or equivalent); imports state file
  <feature>_screen.dart
```

Example: `apps/explorer/lib/features/list/state/`.

## State file

- Holds the immutable `*State` class, `copyWith`, and feature-specific enums (e.g. `CharactersListStatus`).
- No Flutter widgets, no `ChangeNotifier`, no use-case or repository calls.

## Provider file

- Extends `ChangeNotifier` (or the app’s chosen notifier base); owns `_state`, `state` getter, and `_emit`.
- Imports the matching `*_state.dart`; does **not** define state classes inline.
- Calls use cases / repositories only here—not from screens or widgets.

## Screens and DI

- Screens import `state/<feature>_provider.dart` (not a barrel).
- Router / injector registers the provider from `state/` and wraps routes with the required providers.

## Tests

Mirror under `test/features/<feature>/state/` (see `test-mirrors-lib`):

```
lib/features/list/state/characters_list_provider.dart
  → test/features/list/state/characters_list_provider_test.dart
```

## Do not

- Combine state + provider in one file for new or moved features
- Put mutable public fields on the provider—use `state` + `copyWith`
- Import `sl` or repositories from screens (router/DI wraps providers)
